  <div class="step-label">Step 1 of 3</div>
  <h2 style="margin-bottom:1rem">🚫 No computer. We work with the booth.</h2>

  <p>Most "dead" USBs at the booth are a connection or slot issue, not a dead drive. Fastest checks first:</p>

  <ul class="checklist">
    <li><strong>Pull the USB out and reseat it firmly.</strong> Wait 10 seconds before re-inserting.</li>
    <li>Try the <strong>other USB slot</strong> on the same player (if it has two).</li>
    <li>Try the <strong>other player</strong>. If it reads there, play from that deck and use Link.</li>
    <li>Check the USB tip for <strong>dirt or sweat</strong>, wipe it, try again.</li>
  </ul>

  <p class="question">Does any player read the USB now?</p>

  <Choice step="no_laptop_1"
    a={{ href: '/saved?path=critical&branch=no_laptop', label: "YES - IT'S READING", event: 'outcome_reached', data: { outcome: 'saved', path: 'critical' } }}
    b={{ href: '/protocol/critical/no-laptop-2', label: 'NO - STILL NOTHING' }}
  />
</Tunnel>
